      "program_name": "Prohousing Designation, Prohousing Incentive Program applications and City-owned sites for affordable housing (295 South Mathilda Avenue)",
      "administering_agency": "City of Sunnyvale Community Development Department, Housing Division",
      "funding_type": "policy/designation",
      "typical_award_size": "HCD issued Sunnyvale a Prohousing Designation award letter on May 27, 2025 after a December 9, 2024 application (Housing Element Program H41); the City planned a PIP Round 4 application (due March 31, 2026) for homeless services, outreach, shelter and transitional housing activities (award depends on population base and points; Mountain View's comparable request was $890,000). City-owned site: 295 South Mathilda Avenue purchased September 2023 for $7,325,000 and held under an Exclusive Negotiating Agreement (August 30, 2023) and short-term ground lease with MidPen Housing for a 126-unit project with at least 25 percent of units for families experiencing homelessness; the 2024 NOFA awarded $1.5 million for predevelopment; cumulative City support including land about $13.3 million ($105,000 per unit) before construction funds. The City also adopted a water and sewer priority ordinance for affordable developments and received $1.84 million in MTC Housing Incentive Pool funds in 2025.",
      "per_unit_cap": null,
      "affordability_requirement": "295 South Mathilda: 100 percent affordable with 25 percent homeless set-aside; PIP funds for households up to 120 percent AMI.",
